 "about": "Central-bank policy rates in force, percent a year, copied unchanged (USD, EUR, GBP, JPY, AUD only) from research/edge/fx-carry/rates.json on branch fx-carry (commit f9fb1ba28) for the fx-home-hours financing charge. That file says: Central-bank policy rates in force, percent a year, for the fx-carry study. APPROXIMATE AND FROM MEMORY: written out by hand on 14 Nov 2026 from known central-bank decisions, not fetched (FRED and the central banks' hosts are refused by the build network). Each date is the day the new rate took effect (the announcement day, or the next business day after an evening decision) and may be off by a day; a few small moves may be missing or mis-sized. Decisions after mid-2025 are the least certain, and no 2026 decision is recorded: every rate is held at its last listed value through 2026 (check before relying on a 2026 ranking). `check` names the source to verify each line against. `monthEnd` is derived from `decisions` (the rate in force on the last calendar day of each month, in the order of `order`) and tested equal to it.",
